      "audited_unit_ids": []
    },
    {
      "topic": "configuration",
      "statement": "The read structure setup shown here sets PNG_FLAG_BENIGN_ERRORS_WARN when supported and conditionally sets the distinct PNG_FLAG_APP_WARNINGS_WARN. It delegates initial structure creation to png_create_png_struct.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "unit_id": "u-4a3ce9d69b27b864372c",
          "start_line": 24,
          "end_line": 69,
          "role": "dependency",
          "dependency_reason": "These assignments constrain what the visible read setup says about the separate PNG_FLAG_APP_ERRORS_WARN state."
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "u-cc1e0b2b98d159b17936",
          "start_line": 24,
          "end_line": 69,
          "role": "dependency",
          "dependency_reason": "The same visible read setup and delegation appear on the after version."
        }
      ],
      "absence_claim": false,
      "audited_unit_ids": []
    },
    {
      "topic": "configuration",
      "statement": "The supplied build recipe disables the WARNING and WRITE options in pnglibconf.dfa, runs configure, builds libpng16.la, and links the fuzzer with libpng16.a and zlib. These lines do not state the initial PNG_FLAG_APP_ERRORS_WARN value.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "unit_id": "u-d102cd4502b9fe57a4ec",
          "start_line": 25,
          "end_line": 43,
          "role": "dependency",
          "dependency_reason": "The recipe fixes the target's build configuration and linked library."
        }
      ],
      "absence_claim": false,
      "audited_unit_ids": []
    },
    {
      "topic": "alternative",
      "statement": "png_read_row itself calls png_read_start_row if PNG_FLAG_ROW_INIT is clear, providing a row initialization route. The fixed harness nevertheless calls png_start_read_image before its row loop.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "unit_id": "u-f907d51074ecef0236f2",
          "start_line": 382,
          "end_line": 405,
          "role": "primary",
